                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1b6923f9-a0cf-3fb8-898f-927c9571e23c",
                        "entry_id": "efaef015-9b3a-3816-8c86-cd3b05112f33",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sorte d'écharpe, formant un capuchon pour la tête, avec des bouts pendants munis de houppes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b3790cf-dacd-4168-8e87-ba7885de9d93",
                                "sense_id": "1b6923f9-a0cf-3fb8-898f-927c9571e23c",
                                "text": "Les cavaliers ne se couvrent parfois que la gorge, car le chic de la mode locale veut qu'on laisse pendre au vent les bouts du bachlyk."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d9c7b7a-416e-453a-87e3-e881c3f4df23",
                                "sense_id": "1b6923f9-a0cf-3fb8-898f-927c9571e23c",
                                "text": "L'homme, tête nue, tenait un bachlyk à la main."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "51579d5e-98d1-4cdf-9112-f4dbbeda2fc0",
                        "source_entry_id": "efaef015-9b3a-3816-8c86-cd3b05112f33",
                        "source_sense_id": "1b6923f9-a0cf-3fb8-898f-927c9571e23c",
                        "target_lang_word": "Baschlik",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9f12136f-6ea4-41a3-89a2-661efd99a943",
                        "source_entry_id": "efaef015-9b3a-3816-8c86-cd3b05112f33",
                        "source_sense_id": "1b6923f9-a0cf-3fb8-898f-927c9571e23c",
                        "target_lang_word": "bashlyk",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bashlyk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "178a8bbd-38e7-3d4f-8dd4-8585b430637e",
                                        "entry_id": "70de0d32-5766-3a9b-b640-abb1b92d7b2e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A protective cone-shaped hood with lappets for wrapping around the neck, used especially by Turks and Cossacks."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f97dc409-0f39-444f-a2d4-e6e4f43acaa0",
                                                "sense_id": "178a8bbd-38e7-3d4f-8dd4-8585b430637e",
                                                "text": "In winter the troops wore the grey greatcoat and the bashlyk, a sort of hood protecting the neck and ears."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98074768-8146-4659-a0e5-016362638c83",
                                                "sense_id": "178a8bbd-38e7-3d4f-8dd4-8585b430637e",
                                                "text": "The description of Jews wearing very high hats (\"as tall as themselves\" or \"an amah high\") calls to mind the tall pointed cap, or hood bashlyk brought by the Iranians from the Siberian steppes. The bashlyk occurs with great frequency among the Medean and Persian tribes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20511419-ee33-4ff0-9314-c60f5386497d",
                                                "sense_id": "178a8bbd-38e7-3d4f-8dd4-8585b430637e",
                                                "text": "The obverse bust wears a completely new style of bashlyk, resembling the Macedonian kausia, but with a flap at the back and an eagle on top."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a1b664c-2f70-4cca-adc2-a46b2f1586c1",
                                                "sense_id": "178a8bbd-38e7-3d4f-8dd4-8585b430637e",
                                                "text": "Then one of the strangers mounted the throne, where he took off his bashlyk or cap-like head covering. All of the Lamas fell to their knees as they recognized the man who had been long ago described in the sacred bulls of Dalai Lama, Tashi Lama and Bogdo Khan."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fa13a9d9-3ef6-48b1-9a0e-9a1956c4e715",
                        "source_entry_id": "efaef015-9b3a-3816-8c86-cd3b05112f33",
                        "source_sense_id": "1b6923f9-a0cf-3fb8-898f-927c9571e23c",
                        "target_lang_word": "baszłyk",
                        "target_lang_code": "pl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "baszłyk",
                                "target_lang_code": "pl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc571e43-8405-371b-a876-15b93564c5fe",
                                        "entry_id": "08dfdedc-d208-3092-a3c2-7067bdd01451",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "kaptur z grubej tkaniny, o długich patkach zawiązywanych dookoła szyi"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d1a7789-a3e5-4b01-b56d-9ea5d89376b4",
                                                "sense_id": "fc571e43-8405-371b-a876-15b93564c5fe",
                                                "text": "Kozacy otuleni w baszłyki od czasu do czasu przechodzili w wyciągnięty kłus"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "776bbddb-443f-442f-897b-a5dbc8d8e125",
                                                "sense_id": "fc571e43-8405-371b-a876-15b93564c5fe",
                                                "text": "Wjeżdżali do miasteczka, gdy minęli ośnieżonego człowieka. Usunął się w zaspę. Był ubrany w kożuch i chodaki z łozy, twarz całą zakrywał baszłyk"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1193a855-61bd-4020-ade5-a7727604b339",
                        "source_entry_id": "efaef015-9b3a-3816-8c86-cd3b05112f33",
                        "source_sense_id": "1b6923f9-a0cf-3fb8-898f-927c9571e23c",
